<title>NETHERLANDS: Vendex says has 93.4 pct of BIS.</title>
<headline>Vendex says has 93.4 pct of BIS.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch retailer and employment services company Vendex International NV said on Friday it owned 93.4 pct of the shares in French temporary employment agency BIS.</p>
<p>Vendex said in a statement that at the end of February it had 59.04 percent of BIS shares which it had acquired for 490 francs per share. It bid for the remaining shares on the Paris bourse for the same price, it said on Friday.  </p>
<p>Vendex in January announced its $473 million bid for BIS with the aim of widening its European focus.</p>
<p>The acquisition would more than double annual turnover of Vendex's business services division to more than six billion guilders and create Europe's third largest temporary employment agency.</p>
